{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-is-selective-ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What is Selective SSR?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In TanStack Start, routes matching the initial request are rendered on the server by default. This means "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" are executed on the server, followed by rendering the route components. The resulting HTML is sent to the client, which hydrates the markup into a fully interactive application."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"However, there are cases where you might want to disable SSR for certain routes or all routes, such as:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" requires browser-only APIs (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localStorage"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the route component depends on browser-only APIs (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvas"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start's Selective SSR feature lets you configure:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which routes should execute "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which route components should be rendered on the server."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-does-this-compare-to-spa-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How does this compare to SPA mode?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start's "},{"type":"link","href":"./spa-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SPA mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":" completely disables server-side execution of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":", as well as server-side rendering of route components. Selective SSR allows you to configure server-side handling on a per-route basis, either statically or dynamically."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can control how a route is handled during the initial server request using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr"},{"type":"text","value":" property. If this property is not set, it defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":". You can change this default using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultSsr"},{"type":"text","value":" option in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createStart"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/start.ts\nimport { createStart } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nexport const startInstance = createStart(() => ({\n  // Disable SSR by default\n  defaultSsr: false,\n}))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ssr-true","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: true"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the default behavior unless otherwise configured. On the initial request, it will:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server and send the resulting context to the client."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server and send the loader data to the client."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render the component on the server and send the HTML markup to the client."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  ssr: true,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the server</div>,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ssr-false","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: false"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This disables server-side:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Execution of the route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering of the route component."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  ssr: false,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the client during hydration')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the client during hydration')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the client</div>,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ssr-data-only","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: 'data-only'"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hybrid option will:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server and send the resulting context to the client."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server and send the loader data to the client."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disable server-side rendering of the route component."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  ssr: 'data-only',\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the client</div>,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"functional-form","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Functional Form"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For more flexibility, you can use the functional form of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr"},{"type":"text","value":" property to decide at runtime whether to SSR a route:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/docs/$docType/$docId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/docs/$docType/$docId')({\n  validateSearch: z.object({ details: z.boolean().optional() }),\n  ssr: ({ params, search }) => {\n    if (params.status === 'success' && params.value.docType === 'sheet') {\n      return false\n    }\n    if (search.status === 'success' && search.value.details) {\n      return 'data-only'\n    }\n  },\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server depending on the result of ssr()')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server depending on the result of ssr()')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the client</div>,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr"},{"type":"text","value":" function runs only on the server during the initial request and is stripped from the client bundle."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"search"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params"},{"type":"text","value":" are passed in after validation as a discriminated union:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"params:\n    | { status: 'success'; value: Expand<ResolveAllParamsFromParent<TParentRoute, TParams>> }\n    | { status: 'error'; error: unknown }\nsearch:\n    | { status: 'success'; value: Expand<ResolveFullSearchSchema<TParentRoute, TSearchValidator>> }\n    | { status: 'error'; error: unknown }","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If validation fails, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" will be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":" will contain the failure details. Otherwise, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" will be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"success"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" will contain the validated data."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"inheritance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inheritance"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"At runtime, a child route inherits the Selective SSR configuration of its parent. However, the inherited value can only be changed to be more restrictive (i.e. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data-only"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data-only"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":"). For example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"root { ssr: undefined }\n  posts { ssr: false }\n     $postId { ssr: true }","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"root"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: true"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"posts"},{"type":"text","value":" explicitly sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: false"},{"type":"text","value":", so neither "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" nor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" will run on the server, and the route component won't be rendered on the server."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$postId"},{"type":"text","value":" sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: true"},{"type":"text","value":", but inherits "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: false"},{"type":"text","value":" from its parent. Because the inherited value can only be changed to be more restrictive, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: true"},{"type":"text","value":" has no effect and the inherited "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: false"},{"type":"text","value":" will remain."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Another example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"root { ssr: undefined }\n  posts { ssr: 'data-only' }\n     $postId { ssr: true }\n       details { ssr: false }","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"root"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: true"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"posts"},{"type":"text","value":" sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: 'data-only'"},{"type":"text","value":", so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" run on the server, but the route component isn't rendered on the server."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$postId"},{"type":"text","value":" sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: true"},{"type":"text","value":", but inherits "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: 'data-only'"},{"type":"text","value":" from its parent."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"details"},{"type":"text","value":" sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: false"},{"type":"text","value":", so neither "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" nor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" will run on the server, and the route component won't be rendered on the server. Here the inherited value is changed to be more restrictive, and therefore, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: false"},{"type":"text","value":" will override the inherited value."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"fallback-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fallback Rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the first route with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: false"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ssr: 'data-only'"},{"type":"text","value":", the server will render the route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pendingComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" as a fallback. If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pendingComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" isn't configured, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultPendingComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" will be rendered. If neither is configured, no fallback will be rendered."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the client during hydration, this fallback will be displayed for at least "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"minPendingMs"},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultPendingMinMs"},{"type":"text","value":" if not configured), even if the route doesn't have "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" defined."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-to-disable-ssr-of-the-root-route","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How to disable SSR of the root route?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can disable server side rendering of the root route component, however the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<html>"},{"type":"text","value":" shell still needs to be rendered on the server. This shell is configured via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" property and takes a single property "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" is always SSRed and is wrapping around the root "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component"},{"type":"text","value":", the root "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" or the root "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" component respectively."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A minimal setup of a root route with disabled SSR for the route component looks like this:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import * as React from 'react'\n\nimport {\n  HeadContent,\n  Outlet,\n  Scripts,\n  createRootRoute,\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  shellComponent: RootShell,\n  component: RootComponent,\n  errorComponent: () => <div>Error</div>,\n  notFoundComponent: () => <div>Not found</div>,\n  ssr: false, // or `defaultSsr: false` on the router\n})\n\nfunction RootShell({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <html>\n      <head>\n        <HeadContent />\n      </head>\n      <body>\n        {children}\n        <Scripts />\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction RootComponent() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>This component will be rendered on the client</h1>\n      <Outlet />\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"what-is-selective-ssr","text":"What is Selective SSR?","level":2},{"id":"how-does-this-compare-to-spa-mode","text":"How does this compare to SPA mode?","level":2},{"id":"configuration","text":"Configuration","level":2},{"id":"ssr-true","text":"ssr: true","level":3},{"id":"ssr-false","text":"ssr: false","level":3},{"id":"ssr-data-only","text":"ssr: 'data-only'","level":3},{"id":"functional-form","text":"Functional Form","level":3},{"id":"inheritance","text":"Inheritance","level":3},{"id":"fallback-rendering","text":"Fallback Rendering","level":2},{"id":"how-to-disable-ssr-of-the-root-route","text":"How to disable SSR of the root route?","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## What is Selective SSR?\n\nIn TanStack Start, routes matching the initial request are rendered on the server by default. This means `beforeLoad` and `loader` are executed on the server, followed by rendering the route components. The resulting HTML is sent to the client, which hydrates the markup into a fully interactive application.\n\nHowever, there are cases where you might want to disable SSR for certain routes or all routes, such as:\n\n- When `beforeLoad` or `loader` requires browser-only APIs (e.g., `localStorage`).\n- When the route component depends on browser-only APIs (e.g., `canvas`).\n\nTanStack Start's Selective SSR feature lets you configure:\n\n- Which routes should execute `beforeLoad` or `loader` on the server.\n- Which route components should be rendered on the server.\n\n## How does this compare to SPA mode?\n\nTanStack Start's [SPA mode](./spa-mode) completely disables server-side execution of `beforeLoad` and `loader`, as well as server-side rendering of route components. Selective SSR allows you to configure server-side handling on a per-route basis, either statically or dynamically.\n\n## Configuration\n\nYou can control how a route is handled during the initial server request using the `ssr` property. If this property is not set, it defaults to `true`. You can change this default using the `defaultSsr` option in `createStart`:\n\n```tsx\n// src/start.ts\nimport { createStart } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nexport const startInstance = createStart(() => ({\n  // Disable SSR by default\n  defaultSsr: false,\n}))\n```\n\n### `ssr: true`\n\nThis is the default behavior unless otherwise configured. On the initial request, it will:\n\n- Run `beforeLoad` on the server and send the resulting context to the client.\n- Run `loader` on the server and send the loader data to the client.\n- Render the component on the server and send the HTML markup to the client.\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  ssr: true,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the server</div>,\n})\n```\n\n### `ssr: false`\n\nThis disables server-side:\n\n- Execution of the route's `beforeLoad` and `loader`.\n- Rendering of the route component.\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  ssr: false,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the client during hydration')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the client during hydration')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the client</div>,\n})\n```\n\n### `ssr: 'data-only'`\n\nThis hybrid option will:\n\n- Run `beforeLoad` on the server and send the resulting context to the client.\n- Run `loader` on the server and send the loader data to the client.\n- Disable server-side rendering of the route component.\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  ssr: 'data-only',\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the client</div>,\n})\n```\n\n### Functional Form\n\nFor more flexibility, you can use the functional form of the `ssr` property to decide at runtime whether to SSR a route:\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/docs/$docType/$docId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/docs/$docType/$docId')({\n  validateSearch: z.object({ details: z.boolean().optional() }),\n  ssr: ({ params, search }) => {\n    if (params.status === 'success' && params.value.docType === 'sheet') {\n      return false\n    }\n    if (search.status === 'success' && search.value.details) {\n      return 'data-only'\n    }\n  },\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server depending on the result of ssr()')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server depending on the result of ssr()')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the client</div>,\n})\n```\n\nThe `ssr` function runs only on the server during the initial request and is stripped from the client bundle.\n\n`search` and `params` are passed in after validation as a discriminated union:\n\n```tsx\nparams:\n    | { status: 'success'; value: Expand<ResolveAllParamsFromParent<TParentRoute, TParams>> }\n    | { status: 'error'; error: unknown }\nsearch:\n    | { status: 'success'; value: Expand<ResolveFullSearchSchema<TParentRoute, TSearchValidator>> }\n    | { status: 'error'; error: unknown }\n```\n\nIf validation fails, `status` will be `error` and `error` will contain the failure details. Otherwise, `status` will be `success` and `value` will contain the validated data.\n\n### Inheritance\n\nAt runtime, a child route inherits the Selective SSR configuration of its parent. However, the inherited value can only be changed to be more restrictive (i.e. `true` to `data-only` or `false` and `data-only` to `false`). For example:\n\n```tsx\nroot { ssr: undefined }\n  posts { ssr: false }\n     $postId { ssr: true }\n```\n\n- `root` defaults to `ssr: true`.\n- `posts` explicitly sets `ssr: false`, so neither `beforeLoad` nor `loader` will run on the server, and the route component won't be rendered on the server.\n- `$postId` sets `ssr: true`, but inherits `ssr: false` from its parent. Because the inherited value can only be changed to be more restrictive, `ssr: true` has no effect and the inherited `ssr: false` will remain.\n\nAnother example:\n\n```tsx\nroot { ssr: undefined }\n  posts { ssr: 'data-only' }\n     $postId { ssr: true }\n       details { ssr: false }\n```\n\n- `root` defaults to `ssr: true`.\n- `posts` sets `ssr: 'data-only'`, so `beforeLoad` and `loader` run on the server, but the route component isn't rendered on the server.\n- `$postId` sets `ssr: true`, but inherits `ssr: 'data-only'` from its parent.\n- `details` sets `ssr: false`, so neither `beforeLoad` nor `loader` will run on the server, and the route component won't be rendered on the server. Here the inherited value is changed to be more restrictive, and therefore, the `ssr: false` will override the inherited value.\n\n## Fallback Rendering\n\nFor the first route with `ssr: false` or `ssr: 'data-only'`, the server will render the route's `pendingComponent` as a fallback. If `pendingComponent` isn't configured, the `defaultPendingComponent` will be rendered. If neither is configured, no fallback will be rendered.\n\nOn the client during hydration, this fallback will be displayed for at least `minPendingMs` (or `defaultPendingMinMs` if not configured), even if the route doesn't have `beforeLoad` or `loader` defined.\n\n## How to disable SSR of the root route?\n\nYou can disable server side rendering of the root route component, however the `<html>` shell still needs to be rendered on the server. This shell is configured via the `shellComponent` property and takes a single property `children`. The `shellComponent` is always SSRed and is wrapping around the root `component`, the root `errorComponent` or the root `notFound` component respectively.\n\nA minimal setup of a root route with disabled SSR for the route component looks like this:\n\n```tsx\nimport * as React from 'react'\n\nimport {\n  HeadContent,\n  Outlet,\n  Scripts,\n  createRootRoute,\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  shellComponent: RootShell,\n  component: RootComponent,\n  errorComponent: () => <div>Error</div>,\n  notFoundComponent: () => <div>Not found</div>,\n  ssr: false, // or `defaultSsr: false` on the router\n})\n\nfunction RootShell({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <html>\n      <head>\n        <HeadContent />\n      </head>\n      <body>\n        {children}\n        <Scripts />\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction RootComponent() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>This component will be rendered on the client</h1>\n      <Outlet />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: selective-ssr\ntitle: Selective Server-Side Rendering (SSR)\n---\n\n## What is Selective SSR?\n\nIn TanStack Start, routes matching the initial request are rendered on the server by default. This means `beforeLoad` and `loader` are executed on the server, followed by rendering the route components. The resulting HTML is sent to the client, which hydrates the markup into a fully interactive application.\n\nHowever, there are cases where you might want to disable SSR for certain routes or all routes, such as:\n\n- When `beforeLoad` or `loader` requires browser-only APIs (e.g., `localStorage`).\n- When the route component depends on browser-only APIs (e.g., `canvas`).\n\nTanStack Start's Selective SSR feature lets you configure:\n\n- Which routes should execute `beforeLoad` or `loader` on the server.\n- Which route components should be rendered on the server.\n\n## How does this compare to SPA mode?\n\nTanStack Start's [SPA mode](./spa-mode) completely disables server-side execution of `beforeLoad` and `loader`, as well as server-side rendering of route components. Selective SSR allows you to configure server-side handling on a per-route basis, either statically or dynamically.\n\n## Configuration\n\nYou can control how a route is handled during the initial server request using the `ssr` property. If this property is not set, it defaults to `true`. You can change this default using the `defaultSsr` option in `createStart`:\n\n```tsx\n// src/start.ts\nimport { createStart } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nexport const startInstance = createStart(() => ({\n  // Disable SSR by default\n  defaultSsr: false,\n}))\n```\n\n### `ssr: true`\n\nThis is the default behavior unless otherwise configured. On the initial request, it will:\n\n- Run `beforeLoad` on the server and send the resulting context to the client.\n- Run `loader` on the server and send the loader data to the client.\n- Render the component on the server and send the HTML markup to the client.\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  ssr: true,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the server</div>,\n})\n```\n\n### `ssr: false`\n\nThis disables server-side:\n\n- Execution of the route's `beforeLoad` and `loader`.\n- Rendering of the route component.\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  ssr: false,\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the client during hydration')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the client during hydration')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the client</div>,\n})\n```\n\n### `ssr: 'data-only'`\n\nThis hybrid option will:\n\n- Run `beforeLoad` on the server and send the resulting context to the client.\n- Run `loader` on the server and send the loader data to the client.\n- Disable server-side rendering of the route component.\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/posts/$postId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  ssr: 'data-only',\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server during the initial request')\n    console.log('Executes on the client for subsequent navigation')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the client</div>,\n})\n```\n\n### Functional Form\n\nFor more flexibility, you can use the functional form of the `ssr` property to decide at runtime whether to SSR a route:\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/docs/$docType/$docId.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/docs/$docType/$docId')({\n  validateSearch: z.object({ details: z.boolean().optional() }),\n  ssr: ({ params, search }) => {\n    if (params.status === 'success' && params.value.docType === 'sheet') {\n      return false\n    }\n    if (search.status === 'success' && search.value.details) {\n      return 'data-only'\n    }\n  },\n  beforeLoad: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server depending on the result of ssr()')\n  },\n  loader: () => {\n    console.log('Executes on the server depending on the result of ssr()')\n  },\n  component: () => <div>This component is rendered on the client</div>,\n})\n```\n\nThe `ssr` function runs only on the server during the initial request and is stripped from the client bundle.\n\n`search` and `params` are passed in after validation as a discriminated union:\n\n```tsx\nparams:\n    | { status: 'success'; value: Expand<ResolveAllParamsFromParent<TParentRoute, TParams>> }\n    | { status: 'error'; error: unknown }\nsearch:\n    | { status: 'success'; value: Expand<ResolveFullSearchSchema<TParentRoute, TSearchValidator>> }\n    | { status: 'error'; error: unknown }\n```\n\nIf validation fails, `status` will be `error` and `error` will contain the failure details. Otherwise, `status` will be `success` and `value` will contain the validated data.\n\n### Inheritance\n\nAt runtime, a child route inherits the Selective SSR configuration of its parent. However, the inherited value can only be changed to be more restrictive (i.e. `true` to `data-only` or `false` and `data-only` to `false`). For example:\n\n```tsx\nroot { ssr: undefined }\n  posts { ssr: false }\n     $postId { ssr: true }\n```\n\n- `root` defaults to `ssr: true`.\n- `posts` explicitly sets `ssr: false`, so neither `beforeLoad` nor `loader` will run on the server, and the route component won't be rendered on the server.\n- `$postId` sets `ssr: true`, but inherits `ssr: false` from its parent. Because the inherited value can only be changed to be more restrictive, `ssr: true` has no effect and the inherited `ssr: false` will remain.\n\nAnother example:\n\n```tsx\nroot { ssr: undefined }\n  posts { ssr: 'data-only' }\n     $postId { ssr: true }\n       details { ssr: false }\n```\n\n- `root` defaults to `ssr: true`.\n- `posts` sets `ssr: 'data-only'`, so `beforeLoad` and `loader` run on the server, but the route component isn't rendered on the server.\n- `$postId` sets `ssr: true`, but inherits `ssr: 'data-only'` from its parent.\n- `details` sets `ssr: false`, so neither `beforeLoad` nor `loader` will run on the server, and the route component won't be rendered on the server. Here the inherited value is changed to be more restrictive, and therefore, the `ssr: false` will override the inherited value.\n\n## Fallback Rendering\n\nFor the first route with `ssr: false` or `ssr: 'data-only'`, the server will render the route's `pendingComponent` as a fallback. If `pendingComponent` isn't configured, the `defaultPendingComponent` will be rendered. If neither is configured, no fallback will be rendered.\n\nOn the client during hydration, this fallback will be displayed for at least `minPendingMs` (or `defaultPendingMinMs` if not configured), even if the route doesn't have `beforeLoad` or `loader` defined.\n\n## How to disable SSR of the root route?\n\nYou can disable server side rendering of the root route component, however the `<html>` shell still needs to be rendered on the server. This shell is configured via the `shellComponent` property and takes a single property `children`. The `shellComponent` is always SSRed and is wrapping around the root `component`, the root `errorComponent` or the root `notFound` component respectively.\n\nA minimal setup of a root route with disabled SSR for the route component looks like this:\n\n```tsx\nimport * as React from 'react'\n\nimport {\n  HeadContent,\n  Outlet,\n  Scripts,\n  createRootRoute,\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  shellComponent: RootShell,\n  component: RootComponent,\n  errorComponent: () => <div>Error</div>,\n  notFoundComponent: () => <div>Not found</div>,\n  ssr: false, // or `defaultSsr: false` on the router\n})\n\nfunction RootShell({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <html>\n      <head>\n        <HeadContent />\n      </head>\n      <body>\n        {children}\n        <Scripts />\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction RootComponent() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>This component will be rendered on the client</h1>\n      <Outlet />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
